    "teacher_markdown": "- Students edit only `story_review.txt` on this level. If testing shows a bug, they can go back and fix `main.py`.\r\n- MY TESTING: students work out the total and the average by hand before comparing them with the program. A mismatch is the point of the exercise, not a failure. Ask what they changed.\r\n- MY PARTNER CHECK: the partner guesses the average from the numbers alone. A guess within a few units shows they understand what an average is. Ask the partner how they estimated it.\r\n- MY REFLECTION: look for specifics. Good answers name what students asked AI Tutor to do and one thing they kept, changed, or rejected, with a reason. \"It worked\" is not enough, so ask what they checked.\r\n- Students should name which lines they wrote themselves. The sum and the average should be on that list.\r\n- This level has no Validate.\r\n- Use this level to check whether students can test their code against a hand calculation, explain what an average tells them to a partner, and describe what they kept, changed, or rejected from AI-generated code."
